# Observe Flame Blade's augment form lasting until the caster rests, for bd
# inc-wbq9 (PA-07-F9).
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/flame-blade-augment-duration.keys 1
#
# WHAT IS MEASURED. The `flame blade;augment` effect grants an EXTRA_QUALITY
# stati to a wielded Short/Long Blade with the duration e.vDuration. Before the
# fix that effect carried EF_DXLONG, so e.vDuration = 1000 + 100*level (1100
# turns at level 1). After the fix it carries EF_PERSISTANT, so e.vDuration is
# -2 and lasts until rest. This script casts the plain-blade branch and then
# spends 1200 turns searching, one turn per search, before reading the weapon's
# own page again.
#
# THE ORACLE is the weapon page's quality prose. WQ_FLAMING reads "Flaming"
# (src/Tables.cpp APreQualNames / APostQualNames, line 1564). On a build
# WITHOUT the fix the Flaming quality is gone after the wait; WITH the fix it is
# still there.
@include chargen.keys

# Put the orcish greatsword into the Weapon Hand (plain blade: the augment
# first branch grants it Flaming).
i
f
SPACE
b
SPACE
s
@dump:wielded
ESC

# Wizard mode on.
w
y

# Make Flame Blade castable regardless of class.
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Flame Blade"
ENTER

# Cast Flame Blade on self; answer "Augment or conjure? [aC]" with 'a', then
# choose the greatsword from the item prompt.
m
@choose "Flame Blade"
a
@dump:choose-item
a
@dump:after-cast

# Read the wielded weapon's page before the wait: expect "Flaming".
i
b
x
@dump:weapon-before-wait
ESC
ESC

# Pass 1200 turns without resting. 's' is Search, a full-turn action, and
# Thing::UpdateStati decrements a positive Duration once per creature turn
# (src/Status.cpp:50-60, called from Creature::DoTurn, src/Creature.cpp:1762);
# 1200 exceeds the pre-fix EF_DXLONG duration of 1000 + 100*1.
@until "HP:" ESC
s*1200
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:after-wait

# Read the wielded weapon's page again. Pre-fix: no "Flaming". Post-fix: still
# "Flaming".
i
b
x
@dump:weapon-after-wait
ESC
ESC

@quit
